<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: National Irish Bank cuts fixed rate mortgages.</title>
<headline>National Irish Bank cuts fixed rate mortgages.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Irish Bank said on Wednesday that it was reducing all its fixed rate mortgage products for new customers.</p>
<p>The one-year fixed rate will fall to 6.25 percent from 6.75 percent with effect from October 17.</p>
<p>The bank said it would cut its three-year fixed rate to 7.45 percent and the five-year fixed rate to 7.7 percent, effective from October 23.</p>
<p>National Irish Bank is the Irish subsidiary of National Australia Bank Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
